/**
 * Canonical Skill model — single source of truth for every antman
 * endpoint that returns a skill or a piece of one. These endpoints
 * populate this type today:
 *
 *   - `Aspect.agenticSkills` (catalog view from `POST /v1/apps/definition`)
 *     populates identity-only fields: `id`, `name`, `description`.
 *   - `GET /v1/apps/{appId}/skills` (availability view) populates identity
 *     fields plus `clientHandle` for skills that an app can reference.
 *   - `GET /v1/skills/{skillId}` (full view) populates everything else
 *     (`instructions`, `status`, `type`, `properties`, `tools`, `app`).
 *
 * Different endpoints populate different fields on the same type;
 * every field that isn't required on both views is optional. Same
 * pattern as the canonical `Agent` model.
 *
 * `app` is the owning aspect — present for app-scoped skills, absent
 * for org-scoped skills. The EDK builder today only supports
 * authoring app-scoped skills, so the pull deserializer drops
 * org-scoped skills with a structured miss (the skill body is still
 * readable, but no `skill({...})` source is emitted).
 */
export {};
